# BinderPokedex licensing scope

BinderPokedex separates its software licence from the rights in material used
or reproduced by that software. No single licence covers every element of a
generated PDF, image, or printed binder.

| Material | Applicable terms |
| --- | --- |
| Project program code, including fetchers, rendering code, build scripts, tests, technical configuration, and technical documentation | MIT, unchanged: [LICENSE-CODE](LICENSE-CODE). Commercial use of the software is permitted. Separately identified third-party components retain their own terms. |
| Original, protectable visual expression in `config/templates/cards/classic.svg`, `config/templates/pages/grid_3x3.svg`, and `config/templates/covers/simple.svg` | These creative aspects are designated under [LICENSE-CONTENT.md](LICENSE-CONTENT.md), solely to the extent the project licensor controls the relevant rights. Functional markup, variables, interfaces, and technical implementation remain MIT. A basic grid, dimensions, or layout idea is not claimed as an exclusive project work. |
| Other original human-authored project compositions, visual designs, or creative text, including such contributions reproduced in newly marked PDF/image/print releases | CC BY-NC 4.0 only where expressly identified with this licence in the file, its accompanying notice, or its release manifest, and only for rights the licensor can grant. See [LICENSE-CONTENT.md](LICENSE-CONTENT.md). A generated file is not automatically a protected work or wholly CC-licensed. |
| Pokémon artwork, characters, logos, trademarks, names, factual information, third-party datasets, fonts, and other third-party material | Excluded from the project's content grant. Existing third-party terms and applicable law govern. API availability, a download, or a project notice is not a grant of Pokémon rights. |
| Purely machine-generated or AI-generated material without protectable human authorship | No project copyright or CC restriction is asserted in those elements. Any independently applicable third-party rights or terms remain unaffected. |
| Copies or contributions validly received under an earlier MIT or other licence grant | Those grants remain available on their original terms. This notice does not revoke, narrow, or retroactively replace them. |

The content licence is the unmodified **Creative Commons
Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International** licence; its full text is in
[LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt](LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt). Attribution must be given
in a manner reasonable for the medium and context where that licence applies.
There is no additional advertising-link or platform-specific requirement.

These notices apply prospectively to versions distributed with them. Adding
a notice to an old or unchanged file does not withdraw any valid earlier
permission. Historical releases must be assessed using their actual contents,
applicable rights, and the terms under which they were supplied; this update
does not determine disputed historical licensing questions.

The MIT licence on the renderer does not itself license third-party content
in its output. Conversely, a content notice does not restrict independent use,
modification, sale, or other commercial use of MIT-licensed code. Uses that do
not require the licensor's permission, including statutory exceptions and
limitations, remain unaffected.

See [NOTICE.md](NOTICE.md) for English/German download and attribution guidance.
